    {
      &quot;@id&quot;: &quot;https://www.nidads.com/blog/data-science-analytics-2026#faq&quot;,
      &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;FAQPage&quot;,
      &quot;mainEntity&quot;: [
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is a data science and analytics course?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;A data science and analytics course is a structured programme that teaches Python, SQL, statistics, machine learning, and data visualisation to prepare learners for professional data roles. It typically includes theoretical modules, hands-on projects with real datasets, and career preparation support. Courses range from short certifications (4–12 weeks) to post-graduate programmes (6–12 months).&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Is data science and analytics a good career?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes. Data science and analytics consistently rank among the top career choices globally for salary, growth, and job security. Demand significantly exceeds supply in most markets. India's digital economy, startup ecosystem, and expansion of multinational technology operations have created sustained hiring demand offering high salaries, remote work opportunities, and cross-industry mobility.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What skills are required for analytics?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Core analytics skills: SQL for data querying, Python or R for analysis, statistics for interpretation, and Tableau or Power BI for communicating findings. Critical thinking, problem structuring, and business communication are equally important. Domain knowledge in the target industry significantly increases a candidate's value to employers.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is the salary after a data science and analytics course?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;In India, entry-level data analysts earn ₹3–6 LPA and data scientists earn ₹6–15 LPA. US-based data scientists earn $90,000–$160,000 annually at mid-level. Salary depends on location, company size, specialisation, and tools mastered. Machine learning and AI specialisations command the highest packages globally.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Which tools are used in analytics?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Primary tools: SQL, Python, Tableau, Power BI, Excel, and R. Advanced roles use Apache Spark, BigQuery, and cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure). Tool requirements vary: analysts use SQL and Tableau; scientists use Python and ML libraries; engineers use Spark, Airflow, and cloud infrastructure.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;How long does it take to learn analytics?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;A functional foundation can be built in 3–6 months with consistent daily practice. Job-readiness typically requires 6–12 months including projects and interview preparation. Working professionals completing a data science and analytics course part-time typically take 9–12 months to reach employability.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Can beginners learn data science?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes. Data science is accessible to beginners with no prior programming or mathematics background. Structured learning, consistent practice, and project work are the key requirements. The biggest predictor of success is sustained effort — not prior technical background. Most quality data science and analytics course programmes start from absolute fundamentals.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is the difference between data science and analytics?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Data analytics interprets historical data to identify trends and support decisions. Data science builds predictive models and algorithms to forecast future outcomes. A data science and analytics course trains you in both. Most professionals develop skills in both domains over their careers.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Is Python necessary for data analytics?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Python is not strictly required for entry-level analyst roles, but it significantly expands capabilities. Most mid-to-senior data analytics positions now expect Python proficiency. SQL and Excel remain sufficient for basic reporting. Python enables automation, advanced analysis, and machine learning tasks that differentiate strong candidates.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;How can I get a data analytics internship?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Build a GitHub portfolio with 2–3 complete projects, apply on LinkedIn and Internshala, and prepare for SQL and Python screening tests. Target fintech, edtech, and e-commerce startups where interns receive meaningful work. Freelance analytics projects on Upwork also build experience and references.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        }
      ]
    },
